{"@context":{"name":"https://schema.org/name","description":"https://schema.org/description","level":"fun:level","card":"fun:card","syntax":"fun:syntax","tags":"fun:tags","transfer":"fun:transfer","relations":"fun:relations","examples":"fun:examples"},"@id":"fun:ontology","@graph":[{"@id":"fun:syntax.hello","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Hello world","description":"A Fun script is a sequence of statements; `?.` prints a value and a newline.","level":0,"card":"?. 'Hello, Fun!';","tags":["core","syntax"],"transfer":{"js":"console.log('Hello')","py":"print('Hello')","c":"puts(\"Hello\");"},"intent":["print a value","hello world","打印","输出"],"relations":{"partOf":["fun:syntax.statement"],"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.print"]},"examples":[{"code":"?. 'Hello, Fun!';\n","expect":"Hello, Fun!\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.statement","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Statements and semicolons","description":"Statements end with `;`. The `;` after a block closer (`end if`, `end fun`, `end class`, `end do`, `end loop`, `end try`) is optional, and the last statement before `}` may omit it. Newlines are not statement boundaries.","level":0,"card":"stmt; block ... end block","tags":["core","syntax"],"transfer":{"js":"statement;","py":"one statement per line (Fun does not use indentation)"},"intent":["statement","semicolon","分号","语句"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:pit.newline-is-not-a-statement"]},"examples":[{"code":"var a = 1;\nvar b = a\n  + 2;\n?. b;\n","expect":"3\n"},{"code":"if true then\n  ?. 'ok';\nend if\n?. 'done';\n","expect":"ok\ndone\n"},{"code":"var z = 0;\nif true { z = 1 }\n?. z;\n","expect":"1\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.comment","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Comments","description":"Both `#` and `//` start a line comment. `#* ... #` is a block comment; the next `#` closes it.","level":0,"card":"# line / // line / #* block #","tags":["core","syntax"],"transfer":{"js":"// comment","py":"# comment"},"intent":["comment","注释"],"examples":[{"code":"# a hash comment\n// a slash comment\n#* a block\n   comment #\n?. 1;\n","expect":"1\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.var","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Variables","description":"Declare with `var name = expr;` or `var name;` (nil). There is no `let` or `const`; identifiers are case-insensitive.","level":0,"card":"var x = expr;","tags":["core","syntax"],"transfer":{"js":"let x = 1; const y = 2;","py":"x = 1","c":"int x = 1;"},"intent":["declare a variable","constant","变量","声明"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:sem.case-insensitive","fun:syntax.assignment"]},"examples":[{"code":"var x = 1;\nvar y;\n?. x;\n?. y = nil;\n","expect":"1\nTrue\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.assignment","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Assignment and equality","description":"A statement `x = expr;` assigns; the same `=` inside an expression compares. `<>` and `!=` both mean not-equal. Compound assignment uses `+= -= *= &=`.","level":0,"card":"x = value; if a = b then ...","tags":["core","syntax"],"transfer":{"js":"x = 1; if (a === b)","py":"x = 1; if a == b:","c":"x = 1; if (a == b)"},"intent":["assign","compare","equality","赋值","比较"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:pit.double-equals"]},"examples":[{"code":"var x = 1;\nx = x + 2;\n?. x;\n?. x = 3;\n?. x <> 4;\n","expect":"3\nTrue\nTrue\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.print","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Print and output","description":"Bare `?` prints with no separator, `?.` with a newline, `?,` with a space, and `?:` with a tab. All four accept any value.","level":0,"card":"? value; ?. value;","tags":["core","io"],"transfer":{"js":"console.log(value)","py":"print(value)","c":"printf(\"%v\\n\", value);"},"intent":["print","output","log","输出","打印"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.hello","fun:builtin.tojson"]},"examples":[{"code":"?, 'a';\n?: 'b';\n?. 'c';\n","expect":"a b\tc\n"},{"code":"? 'A';\n? 'B';\n?. '';\n","expect":"AB\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.function","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Named functions","description":"A `fun name(params) ... end fun;` returns the value assigned to `result`; `return expr;` exits early. A one-expression function can also be written `var name(a, b) = expr;`. `result` is not reset on entry, so initialize it explicitly.","level":0,"card":"fun f(a, b) result = a + b; end fun;","tags":["core","function"],"transfer":{"js":"function f(a, b) { return a + b; }","py":"def f(a, b): return a + b","c":"int f(int a, int b) { return a + b; }"},"intent":["define a function","return a value","函数","返回值"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:sem.result","fun:syntax.lambda","fun:sem.named-args"]},"examples":[{"code":"fun add(a, b)\n  result = a + b;\nend fun;\n?. add(2, 3);\n","expect":"5\n"},{"code":"var add(a, b) = a + b;\n?. add(2, 3);\n","expect":"5\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.lambda","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Lambdas","description":"The arrow forms `a -> expr` and `(a, b) -> expr` return an expression. For a block body use `fun (a, b) { ... }` with `return` or `result`; a bare `{ ... }` is a zero-argument block function.","level":0,"card":"f = a -> a * 2;","tags":["core","function"],"transfer":{"js":"a => a * 2","py":"lambda a: a * 2"},"intent":["anonymous function","callback","lambda","匿名函数"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:idiom.pipeline"]},"examples":[{"code":"use 'lib-set.fun';\nvar f = a -> a * 2;\n?. f(3);\nvar nums = [1, 2, 3];\n?. (nums | map(a -> a + 1)).@toJson();\n","expect":"6\n[2,3,4]\n"},{"code":"var g = fun (a, b) { return a * b; };\n?. g(2, 3);\nvar h = { return 9; };\n?. h();\n","expect":"6\n9\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.if","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Conditionals","description":"The form `if c then ... elsif c2 then ... else ... end if;` supports branches. The shorthand `if c { ... }` is a single branch only and takes no `elsif` or `else`.","level":0,"card":"if c then ... end if; / if c { ... }","tags":["core","control"],"transfer":{"js":"if (c) { } else { }","py":"if c: ... else: ..."},"intent":["if","condition","条件"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.case","fun:syntax.brace-block"]},"examples":[{"code":"var n = 2;\nif n = 1 then\n  ?. 'one';\nelsif n = 2 then\n  ?. 'two';\nelse\n  ?. 'other';\nend if;\n","expect":"two\n"},{"code":"var n = 2;\nif n = 2 { ?. 'two'; }\n","expect":"two\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.case","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Case","description":"The form `case expr is when v do ... else ... end case;` matches values.","level":0,"card":"case x is when 1 do ... else ... end case;","tags":["core","control"],"transfer":{"js":"switch (x) { case 1: ... }","py":"match x: case 1: ..."},"intent":["switch","case","分支"],"examples":[{"code":"var x = 2;\ncase x is\n  when 1 do ?. 'one';\n  when 2 do ?. 'two';\n  else ?. 'other';\nend case;\n","expect":"two\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.loop","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Loops","description":"Forms: `for i = a to b do ... end do;`, `for k: v in set do ... end do;`, `while c do ... end do;`, and `loop ... exit when c; ... end loop;`. `while c loop ... end loop;` and `for ... loop ... end loop;` are accepted equivalents; `while c { ... }` and `for ... { ... }` are single-block shorthands. `next when c;` skips.","level":0,"card":"for i = 1 to 3 do ... end do;","tags":["core","control"],"transfer":{"js":"for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {}","py":"for i in range(n):"},"intent":["loop","iterate","for","while","循环","遍历"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.collection","fun:syntax.for-in","fun:syntax.loop-control","fun:syntax.brace-block"]},"examples":[{"code":"var total = 0;\nfor i = 1 to 3 do\n  total += i;\nend do;\n?. total;\nvar m = 0;\nloop\n  m += 1;\n  exit when m >= 2;\nend loop;\n?. m;\n","expect":"6\n2\n"},{"code":"var i = 0;\nwhile i < 2 { i += 1; }\n?. i;\nfor j = 1 to 2 { ?. j; }\n","expect":"2\n1\n2\n"},{"code":"var i = 0;\nwhile i < 2 loop\n  i += 1;\nend loop;\n?. i;\nfor j = 1 to 2 loop\n  ?. j;\nend loop;\n","expect":"2\n1\n2\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.brace-block","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Brace blocks","description":"The forms `if c { ... }`, `while c { ... }` and `for ... { ... }` are shorthand for a single block. The brace `if` takes no `elsif` or `else`; use `then ... end if` when you need branches.","level":1,"card":"if c { ... } / while c { ... } / for ... { ... }","tags":["core","syntax","control"],"transfer":{"js":"if (c) { }","py":"if c: ..."},"intent":["brace block","shorthand","大括号","简写"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.if","fun:syntax.loop","fun:syntax.statement"]},"examples":[{"code":"var n = 2;\nif n = 2 { ?. 'if'; }\n","expect":"if\n"},{"code":"var i = 0;\nwhile i < 2 { i += 1; }\n?. i;\n","expect":"2\n"},{"code":"for j = 1 to 2 { ?. j; }\n","expect":"1\n2\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.for-in","@type":"fun:construct","name":"for-in forms","description":"Four forms: `for v in xs` gives the value, `for v, i in xs` gives value and index, `for k: v in map` gives key and value, and `for k: v, i in map` adds the index. Numeric `for` accepts `step`.","level":1,"card":"for v, i in xs / for k: v, i in map","tags":["core","control","data"],"transfer":{"js":"for (const [i, v] of xs.entries())","py":"for i, v in enumerate(xs)"},"intent":["iterate","for in","index","key value","遍历","索引"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.loop","fun:syntax.brace-block"]},"examples":[{"code":"var xs = ['a', 'b'];\nfor v in xs do ?. v; end do;\nfor v, i in xs do ?. v & i; end do;\nvar m = new [a: 1, b: 2];\nfor k: v, i in m do ?. k & v & i; end do;\n","expect":"a\nb\na0\nb1\na10\nb21\n"},{"code":"for j = 1 to 3 step 2 do ?. j; end do;\n","expect":"1\n3\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.loop-control","@type":"fun:construct","name":"exit and next","description":"The commands `exit` and `next` leave the innermost loop or skip to the next iteration. Add `when c` to make either conditional.","level":1,"card":"exit when c; next when c;","tags":["core","control"],"transfer":{"js":"break; continue;","py":"break; continue"},"intent":["break","continue","exit","next","跳出循环","继续"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.loop"]},"examples":[{"code":"var n = 0;\nloop\n  n += 1;\n  next when n = 1;\n  exit when n >= 3;\nend loop;\n?. n;\n","expect":"3\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.operators","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Operators","description":"Arithmetic `+ - * / ^ div mod`; comparison `= <> != < <= > >=`; logic `and or not`; string `&`; membership `in`; bitwise `bit and/or/xor`, `bit not`, `<< >>`; regex `=~ !~`. `^` is power, and `div`/`mod` are integer division and remainder.","level":1,"card":"^ div mod in bit and/or/xor << >>","tags":["core","syntax","operators"],"transfer":{"js":"** % & | ^ << >>","py":"** // % & | ^ << >>"},"intent":["operator","power","modulo","bitwise","运算符","位运算"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.assignment","fun:syntax.pipe","fun:syntax.regex"]},"examples":[{"code":"?. (2 ^ 3);\n?. (7 div 2);\n?. (7 mod 2);\n?. (2 in [1, 2, 3]);\n?. (6 bit and 3);\n?. (6 bit or 3);\n?. (6 bit xor 3);\n?. (1 << 3);\n?. (8 >> 2);\n","expect":"8\n3\n1\nTrue\n2\n7\n5\n8\n2\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.try","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Errors","description":"The form `try ... except ... finally ... end try;` catches `raise` and runtime errors. `runtime.lastError()` exposes message, file, line and stack.","level":0,"card":"try ... except ... end try;","tags":["core","error"],"transfer":{"js":"try { } catch (e) { }","py":"try: ... except Exception as e: ..."},"intent":["error handling","exception","异常","错误处理"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:module.runtime"]},"examples":[{"code":"try\n  raise 'boom';\nexcept\n  ?. 'caught';\nend try;\n","expect":"caught\n"},{"code":"try\n  ?. 'body';\nfinally\n  ?. 'cleanup';\nend try;\n","expect":"body\ncleanup\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.class","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Classes","description":"A `class Name(params) ... end class;` body runs as the constructor; `var` fields become members, `fun` declarations become methods, `this` is the instance and `base` the parent. Inherit with `class Child = Parent()`.","level":0,"card":"class C(x) var x = x; fun get() result = x; end fun; end class;","tags":["core","object"],"transfer":{"js":"class C { constructor(x) { this.x = x; } }","py":"class C: def __init__(self, x): self.x = x"},"intent":["class","object","constructor","类","对象"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.operator"]},"examples":[{"code":"class Point(x, y)\n  var x = x;\n  var y = y;\n  fun sum() result = x + y; end fun;\nend class;\nvar p = Point(2, 3);\n?. p.sum();\n?. p.x;\n","expect":"5\n2\n"},{"code":"class Animal(name)\n  var name = name;\n  fun speak() result = name & ' makes a sound'; end fun;\nend class;\nclass Dog = Animal()\n  fun speak() result = base.speak() & ' woof'; end fun;\nend class;\nvar d = Dog('Rex');\n?. d.speak();\n","expect":"Rex makes a sound woof\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.use","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Modules","description":"The statement `use 'lib-set.fun';` links a module by file name; `use 'x.fun' as ns;` namespaces it. Paths resolve relative to the script and the runtime `lib/` directory.","level":0,"card":"use 'lib-set.fun';","tags":["core","module"],"transfer":{"js":"import x from './x.js'","py":"import x","c":"#include \"x.h\""},"intent":["import","module","library","导入","模块"],"relations":{"partOf":["fun:tool.funcmd"]},"examples":[{"code":"use 'lib-set.fun';\nvar xs = [1, 2, 3];\n?. (xs | map(a -> a * 2)).@toJson();\n","expect":"[2,4,6]\n"},{"code":"use 'lib-set.fun' as s;\n?. s.filter([1, 2, 3], a -> a > 1).@toJson();\n","expect":"[2,3]\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.collection","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Lists and maps","description":"A list literal `[1, 2, 3]` is a list. `new [k: v]` is a string-keyed map (called a set in Fun); `new []` is an empty map, while `new [1, 2]` builds a fresh list. Both support `@count`, `@has`, `@add`, and JSON conversion.","level":0,"card":"var xs = [1,2]; var m = new [a: 1];","tags":["core","data"],"transfer":{"js":"[1, 2]; {a: 1}","py":"[1, 2]; {'a': 1}","c":"int a[2] = {1, 2};"},"intent":["list","array","map","dictionary","set","数组","字典","集合"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:sem.reference","fun:idiom.accumulator"]},"examples":[{"code":"var xs = [1, 2, 3];\nvar m = new [name: 'Ada'];\n?. xs.@count();\n?. m.name;\n?. m['name'];\nxs.@add(4);\n?. xs.@toJson();\n","expect":"3\nAda\nAda\n[1,2,3,4]\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.member","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Member access","description":"Forms `obj.key`, `obj['key']` and `obj.['1']` read members; a missing member compares equal to nil. Postfix `?` makes a member or its base optional: `x?.k?`.","level":0,"card":"obj.key / obj['key'] / a?.k?","tags":["core","syntax"],"transfer":{"js":"obj.key; obj['key']; a?.k","py":"obj.key; obj['key']"},"intent":["property","field","index","成员","索引"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:sem.missing-is-nil","fun:pit.optional-chain"]},"examples":[{"code":"var m = new [name: 'Ada'];\n?. m.name;\n?. m['name'];\n?. m.missing = nil;\nvar none = nil;\n?. none?.name? = nil;\n","expect":"Ada\nAda\nTrue\nTrue\n"},{"code":"var m = new ['1': 'one'];\n?. m['1'] = nil;\n?. m.['1'];\n","expect":"True\none\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.method","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Built-in methods","description":"Engine-provided methods use `@`: `x.@toJson()`, `s.@count()`, `m.@('group')`. Methods you write in a class are called without `@`.","level":0,"card":"value.@builtin(); obj.userMethod();","tags":["core","syntax"],"transfer":{"js":"value.toString()","py":"len(value)"},"intent":["built-in method","toJson","count","内建方法"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:builtin.tojson","fun:sem.user-vs-builtin"]},"examples":[{"code":"var xs = [1, 2, 3];\n?. xs.@count();\n?. xs.@toJson();\n","expect":"3\n[1,2,3]\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.ref-arg","@type":"fun:construct","name":"By-reference arguments","description":"At the call site `f(var x)` passes a variable by reference, so assignments in `f` update the caller. The declaration stays `fun f(x)`; only the call adds `var`.","level":2,"card":"f(var x);","tags":["core","function"],"transfer":{"js":"no direct equivalent; objects are shared, rebinding is local","py":"no direct equivalent; rebinding is local","c":"f(&x)"},"intent":["by reference","out parameter","var argument","引用参数"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.function"]},"examples":[{"code":"fun bump(x)\n  x += 1;\nend fun;\nvar n = 1;\nbump(var n);\n?. n;\n","expect":"2\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.time","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Time literals","description":"A time literal is `@'YYYY-MM-DD'` or `@'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS'`; its type is 7. Use `.format(pattern)` for a stable string: the default text is short, with the year last.","level":2,"card":"var d = @'2026-11-24'; d.format('yyyy-MM-dd');","tags":["core","data"],"transfer":{"js":"new Date('2026-11-24')","py":"datetime.date(2026, 11, 24)"},"intent":["date","time","时间","日期"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:sem.type"]},"examples":[{"code":"var d = @'2026-11-24 12:34:56';\n?. d.type();\n?. d.format('yyyy-MM-dd');\n","expect":"7\n2026-11-24\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.pipe","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Pipe","description":"The pipe `value | f` passes the value as the last argument of `f`. `map(f)` takes the list last, so it composes; `filter(list, f)` takes the list first, so call it directly.","level":0,"card":"xs | map(f) | filter(p)","tags":["core","functional"],"transfer":{"js":"xs.map(f).filter(p)","py":"filter(p, map(f, xs))"},"intent":["pipeline","chain","管道"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:idiom.pipeline","fun:syntax.lambda"]},"examples":[{"code":"use 'lib-set.fun';\nvar xs = [1, 2, 3, 4];\nvar ys = xs | map(a -> a * 10);\n?. ys.@toJson();\n","expect":"[10,20,30,40]\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.string","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Strings","description":"Single, double and backtick quotes all delimit strings. Literals do not decode backslash escapes; call `.escape()` to decode `\\n`, `\\t`, etc., use `10.toChar()`, or use a multiline backtick string. `$name` interpolation is done by `.eval()`.","level":0,"card":"'a\\nb'.escape() / backtick multiline","tags":["core","text"],"transfer":{"js":"\"a\\nb\"","py":"\"a\\nb\""},"intent":["string","escape","interpolation","字符串","转义"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:pit.backslash-escape","fun:builtin.escape"]},"examples":[{"code":"var a = 'x\\ny'.escape();\n?. a.length();\nvar b = 'hello';\n?. 'say $b'.eval();\nvar c = 'one' & 10.toChar() & 'two';\n?. c;\n","expect":"3\nsay hello\none\ntwo\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.regex","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Regular expressions","description":"Regex literals are `/pattern/flags`, `%pattern%flags` or `$'pattern'flags`. Use `=~` / `!~` to test, `.match()` to extract, `.replace()` to rewrite.","level":0,"card":"s.match(/\\d+/g); s.replace(/\\d+/g, fn); s =~ /^a/","tags":["core","text"],"transfer":{"js":"s.match(/\\d+/g)","py":"re.findall(r'\\d+', s)"},"intent":["regex","match","replace","正则"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:pit.match-group"]},"examples":[{"code":"var s = 'a1b22';\n?. s.match(/\\d+/g).@toJson();\n?. s.replace(/\\d+/g, (m) -> '[' & m.@(0) & ']');\n?. (s =~ /^a/) <> nil;\n","expect":"[\"1\",\"22\"]\na[1]b[22]\nTrue\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.json","@type":"fun:construct","name":"JSON","description":"The built-in `value.@toJson()` emits JSON; `value.@toJson(json: true)` quotes keys. Parse with `text.getJson(json: true)`. `text.getJson(fd: true)` parses FD.","level":0,"card":"s.getJson(json: true); v.@toJson(json: true);","tags":["core","data"],"transfer":{"js":"JSON.parse(s); JSON.stringify(v)","py":"json.loads(s); json.dumps(v)"},"intent":["json parse","json stringify","JSON","解析JSON"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.fd","fun:module.lib-json"]},"examples":[{"code":"var m = '{\"a\": 1, \"b\": [2, 3]}'.getJson(json: true);\n?. m.a;\n?. m.b[1];\n?. m.@toJson(json: true);\n","expect":"1\n3\n{\"a\":1,\"b\":[2,3]}\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.fd","@type":"fun:construct","name":"FD data","description":"FD is Fun's indentation data notation: `key value` lines, `- item` lists, no braces. `text.getJson(fd: true)` parses it and `value.@toJson(fd: true)` emits it.","level":0,"card":"s.getJson(fd: true); v.@toJson(fd: true);","tags":["core","data"],"transfer":{"js":"YAML-like nested objects","py":"dict / list"},"intent":["fd","configuration","data format","配置","数据格式"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:module.lib-fd","fun:syntax.json"]},"examples":[{"code":"var s = 'name Ada' & 10.toChar() & 'tags' & 10.toChar() & '  - math' & 10.toChar() & '  - code';\nvar m = s.getJson(fd: true);\n?. m.name;\n?. m.tags.@count();\n","expect":"Ada\n2\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:sem.missing-is-nil","@type":"fun:semantic","name":"Missing values compare to nil","description":"Reading a missing member, key or index yields a value that compares equal to nil. This makes `if x = nil then x = init; end if` safe.","level":0,"card":"missing = nil -> True","tags":["semantic","nil"],"transfer":{"js":"undefined == null","py":"None"},"intent":["undefined",null,"missing","未定义","空值"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:pit.missing-key-accumulate","fun:sem.nil-arithmetic"]},"examples":[{"code":"var m = new [];\n?. m.nope = nil;\n?. m['nope'] = nil;\n?. m[0] = nil;\n","expect":"True\nTrue\nTrue\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:sem.nil-arithmetic","@type":"fun:semantic","name":"nil acts as zero in arithmetic","description":"A nil operand in `+ - * / div mod` is treated as 0, and as '' for strings. `x += 1` therefore works on a fresh key. The flip side is that a missing value also compares equal to 0.","level":0,"card":"nil + 1 -> 1; x += 1 works on a fresh key","tags":["semantic","nil","pitfall"],"transfer":{"js":"undefined + 1 -> NaN","py":"None + 1 -> TypeError"},"intent":["nil arithmetic","accumulator","空值运算","累加"],"relations":{"fixedBy":["fun:idiom.accumulator"],"seeAlso":["fun:sem.or-value"]},"examples":[{"code":"var m = new [];\nm.k += 1;\n?. m.k;\nvar z;\n?. z + 1;\n?. m.@has('k');\n?. m.@has('no');\n","expect":"1\n1\nTrue\nFalse\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:sem.or-value","@type":"fun:semantic","name":"or/and return values","description":"Operators `or` and `and` return one of their operands, Lua style: `nil or 5` is 5, `7 or 5` is 7. This powers default values.","level":0,"card":"x = x or default;","tags":["semantic"],"transfer":{"js":"x ?? default","py":"x if x is not None else default"},"intent":["default value","or","默认值"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:idiom.default","fun:sem.nil-arithmetic"]},"examples":[{"code":"?. (nil or 5);\n?. (7 or 5);\n?. (nil and 5) = nil;\n","expect":"5\n7\nTrue\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:sem.result","@type":"fun:semantic","name":"result is not reset","description":"Each function has one `result` slot. It is not cleared on entry, so a call at the same stack depth can see the previous value. Always initialize `result`.","level":0,"card":"fun f() result = 0; ... end fun;","tags":["semantic","pitfall"],"transfer":{"js":"return undefined by default","py":"return None by default"},"intent":["return value","result","返回值"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.function"]},"examples":[{"code":"fun f(n)\n  if n > 0 then result = n; end if;\nend fun;\n?. f(1);\n?. f(0);\nfun g(n)\n  result = 0;\n  if n > 0 then result = n; end if;\nend fun;\n?. g(1);\n?. g(0);\n","expect":"1\n1\n1\n0\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:sem.case-insensitive","@type":"fun:semantic","name":"Identifiers are case-insensitive","description":"Variables, functions, members and built-in method names all fold case. Avoid local names that differ from another symbol only by case.","level":0,"card":"Foo = foo; o.NAME = o.name;","tags":["semantic","pitfall"],"transfer":{"js":"case-sensitive","py":"case-sensitive"},"intent":["case sensitivity","大小写"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.var"]},"examples":[{"code":"var Foo = 1;\n?. foo;\nvar m = new [name: 'Ada'];\n?. m.NAME;\n?. 'Hi'.UPPER();\n","expect":"1\nAda\nHI\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:sem.named-args","@type":"fun:semantic","name":"Named arguments","description":"Call sites may name arguments: `f(b: 2, a: 1)`. Missing arguments are nil, so defaults are written as `if p = nil then p = default; end if`.","level":0,"card":"f(b: 2, a: 1)","tags":["semantic","function"],"transfer":{"js":"f({a: 1, b: 2})","py":"f(a=1, b=2)"},"intent":["named arguments","default argument","命名参数","默认参数"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.function"]},"examples":[{"code":"fun greet(name, punct)\n  if punct = nil then punct = '!'; end if;\n  result = 'Hi ' & name & punct;\nend fun;\n?. greet('Ada');\n?. greet(punct: '?', name: 'Bob');\n","expect":"Hi Ada!\nHi Bob?\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:sem.type","@type":"fun:semantic","name":"Value types","description":"The method `.type()` returns 0 nil, 3 int, 5 real, 6 currency, 7 time, 8 string, 11 bool, -1 other. Integers are 32-bit unless explicitly 64-bit.","level":1,"card":"x.type() -> 0/3/5/6/7/8/11/-1","tags":["semantic","type"],"transfer":{"js":"typeof x","py":"type(x)"},"intent":["type","typeof","类型"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:module.lib-type"]},"examples":[{"code":"var n = 1;\nvar s = 'x';\nvar z;\nvar b = true;\n?. n.type();\n?. s.type();\n?. z.type();\n?. b.type();\n","expect":"3\n8\n0\n11\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:sem.reference","@type":"fun:semantic","name":"Maps and lists are references","description":"Assigning a map or list copies the reference. Mutating one alias is visible through the other; use `@clone()` for an independent copy.","level":1,"card":"var b = a; b.k = 1; # a.k is 1; use a.@clone()","tags":["semantic","data"],"transfer":{"js":"objects are references","py":"lists/dicts are references"},"intent":["copy","reference","clone","拷贝","引用"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.collection"]},"examples":[{"code":"use 'lib-set.fun';\nvar a = [x: 1];\nvar b = a;\nb.x = 2;\n?. a.x;\nvar c = a.@clone();\nc.x = 3;\n?. a.x;\n?. c.x;\n","expect":"2\n2\n3\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:idiom.default","@type":"fun:idiom","name":"Default value","description":"Use `or` to supply a default for nil or false. `x = x or default;`.","level":0,"card":"name = name or 'anonymous';","tags":["idiom"],"transfer":{"js":"name = name || 'anonymous'","py":"name = name or 'anonymous'"},"intent":["default value","fallback","默认值","兜底"],"relations":{"requires":["fun:sem.or-value"]},"examples":[{"code":"fun greet(name)\n  name = name or 'anonymous';\n  result = 'Hi ' & name;\nend fun;\n?. greet(nil);\n?. greet('Ada');\n","expect":"Hi anonymous\nHi Ada\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:idiom.accumulator","@type":"fun:idiom","name":"Safe accumulator","description":"Seed a counter explicitly when you want the intent to be obvious across builds: `m.k = (m.k or 0) + 1;`. On 9.5.7, `m.k += 1` also yields 1.","level":0,"card":"m.k = (m.k or 0) + 1;","tags":["idiom","pitfall"],"transfer":{"js":"m[k] = (m[k] || 0) + 1","py":"m[k] = m.get(k, 0) + 1"},"intent":["count","counter","accumulate","计数","累加"],"relations":{"requires":["fun:sem.nil-arithmetic"]},"examples":[{"code":"var m = new [];\nm.k = (m.k or 0) + 1;\nm.k = (m.k or 0) + 1;\n?. m.k;\n","expect":"2\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:idiom.pipeline","@type":"fun:idiom","name":"Data pipeline","description":"The pipeline `xs | map(f)` reads left to right. Add `use 'lib-set.fun';` first. `map` takes the list last and composes; `filter` takes the list first.","level":0,"card":"xs | map(f)","tags":["idiom","functional"],"transfer":{"js":"xs.map(f).filter(p)","py":"[...]"},"intent":["transform list","pipeline","列表处理","管道"],"relations":{"requires":["fun:syntax.use"],"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.pipe"]},"examples":[{"code":"use 'lib-set.fun';\nvar xs = [1, 2, 3, 4];\n?. (xs | map(a -> a * a)).@toJson();\n?. filter(xs, a -> a > 2).@toJson();\n","expect":"[1,4,9,16]\n[3,4]\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:idiom.closure","@type":"fun:idiom","name":"Closure counter","description":"A function value captures its defining scope. Capture an argument to build a specialized function without a class.","level":1,"card":"fun adder(n) result = a -> a + n; end fun;","tags":["idiom","function"],"transfer":{"js":"let n = 0; return () => ++n","py":"def counter(): n = 0; ..."},"intent":["closure","partial application","闭包"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.lambda"]},"examples":[{"code":"fun adder(n)\n  result = a -> a + n;\nend fun;\nvar add2 = adder(2);\n?. add2(3);\n?. add2(10);\n","expect":"5\n12\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:idiom.json-roundtrip","@type":"fun:idiom","name":"JSON round trip","description":"Parse with `.getJson(json: true)`, inspect with member access, emit with `.@toJson(json: true)`.","level":0,"card":"var m = s.getJson(json: true); ...; m.@toJson(json: true)","tags":["idiom","json"],"transfer":{"js":"JSON.parse / JSON.stringify","py":"json.loads / json.dumps"},"intent":["parse json","api response","解析JSON"],"relations":{"requires":["fun:syntax.json"]},"examples":[{"code":"var s = '{\"users\": [{\"name\": \"Ada\"}]}';\nvar m = s.getJson(json: true);\n?. m.users[0].name;\nm.users[0].active = true;\n?. m.@toJson(json: true);\n","expect":"Ada\n{\"users\":[{\"name\":\"Ada\",\"active\":true}]}\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:idiom.file-io","@type":"fun:idiom","name":"Read and write files","description":"The built-in `'path'.load()` reads a whole file; `'path'.save(text)` writes one. For directories, atomic writes and walking use `use 'fs.fun';`.","level":1,"card":"var s = 'in.txt'.load(); 'out.txt'.save(s);","tags":["idiom","io"],"transfer":{"js":"fs.readFileSync(p, 'utf8')","py":"open(p).read()"},"intent":["read file","write file","读文件","写文件"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:module.fs"]},"examples":[{"code":"use 'fs.fun';\nvar p = fs.tempFile('fun-ontology-');\np.save('hello');\n?. p.load();\nfs.removeAll(p);\n","expect":"hello\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:idiom.cli","@type":"fun:idiom","name":"Command-line arguments","description":"The expression `i.arg()` reads argv by position; `Argv()` (from `lib-cmdline`) returns the list. `use 'cli.fun';` gives flags, subcommands and help.","level":1,"card":"var first = 2.arg();","tags":["idiom","cli"],"transfer":{"js":"process.argv","py":"sys.argv"},"intent":["cli","argv","arguments","命令行"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:module.cli"]},"examples":[{"code":"?. 0.arg().length() > 0;\n","expect":"True\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:idiom.ffi","@type":"fun:idiom","name":"Call native code","description":"The call `LibC().getapi(name, signature)` or `'libname'.getapi(...)` binds a native function. The signature is `argtypes:rettype`, e.g. `':i'` for no args returning int.","level":2,"card":"var f = LibC().getapi('getpid', ':i'); f();","tags":["idiom","native"],"transfer":{"c":"#include <unistd.h>; getpid();","js":"native addon"},"intent":["ffi","native call","foreign function","调用C"],"relations":{"requires":["fun:module.lib-host"],"seeAlso":["fun:module.lib-cwinapi","fun:module.lib-cstruct"]},"examples":[{"code":"use 'lib-host.fun';\nvar getpid = LibC().getapi('getpid', ':i');\n?. getpid() > 0;\n","expect":"True\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:pit.double-equals","@type":"fun:pitfall","name":"There is no ==","description":"Use `=` for equality inside an expression, and `<>` or `!=` for inequality. `==` is not Fun.","level":0,"card":"if a = b then ...; if a <> b then ...;","tags":["pitfall","syntax"],"transfer":{"js":"===","py":"==","c":"=="},"intent":["equality","not equal","等于"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.assignment"]},"examples":[{"code":"?. (1 = 1);\n?. (1 <> 2);\n","expect":"True\nTrue\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:pit.newline-is-not-a-statement","@type":"fun:pitfall","name":"Newlines do not end statements","description":"A newline is whitespace. Put `;` between statements; a continuation line can silently join the previous expression.","level":0,"card":"a = 1; b = 2;","tags":["pitfall","syntax"],"transfer":{"js":"automatic semicolon insertion","py":"indentation ends statements"},"intent":["newline","automatic semicolon","换行"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.statement"]},"examples":[{"code":"var a = 1\n  + 2;\n?. a;\n","expect":"3\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:pit.backslash-escape","@type":"fun:pitfall","name":"Literals do not decode backslash escapes","description":"The literal `'\\n'` is a backslash followed by `n`, not a newline. Call `.escape()` to decode it, or use `10.toChar()` or a multiline backtick string.","level":0,"card":"'a\\nb'.escape()","tags":["pitfall","text"],"transfer":{"js":"\"a\\nb\"","py":"\"a\\nb\""},"intent":["newline","escape","换行","转义"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.string","fun:builtin.escape"]},"examples":[{"code":"?. 'a\\nb'.length();\n?. 'a\\nb'.escape().length();\n?. ('a' & 10.toChar() & 'b').length();\n","expect":"4\n3\n3\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:pit.optional-chain","@type":"fun:pitfall","name":"Optional chaining is limited","description":"The form `x?.k?` makes the base and the member optional. It does not make a following call optional, and `f()?.x` is not the JS form; assign to a variable first.","level":1,"card":"a?.k? only","tags":["pitfall","syntax"],"transfer":{"js":"a?.k?.()"},"intent":["optional chaining","null safe","可选链"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.member"]},"examples":[{"code":"fun pick(o, k) result = o?.k?; end fun;\n?. pick(new [k: 7], 'k');\n?. pick(nil, 'k') = nil;\n","expect":"7\nTrue\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:pit.match-group","@type":"fun:pitfall","name":"Regex match group access","description":"In a match object, `m.@(0)` is the whole match and `m.@('name')` a named group; `m.@@()` is also the whole match. `m.@()` with no argument is not valid.","level":1,"card":"m.@(0); m.@('group'); m.@@()","tags":["pitfall","text"],"transfer":{"js":"m[0]","py":"m.group(0)"},"intent":["regex group","capture","正则分组"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.regex"]},"examples":[{"code":"var m = 'a12'.match(/(\\d+)/);\n?. m.@(0);\n?. m.@(1);\n","expect":"12\n12\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:pit.missing-key-accumulate","@type":"fun:pitfall","name":"A missing value also equals zero","description":"A missing value compares equal to nil and to 0, so `if x = 0` cannot tell \"absent\" from \"zero\". Use `.@has(key)` when presence matters.","level":0,"card":"m.@has('k')","tags":["pitfall","data"],"transfer":{"js":"Object.hasOwn(m, k)","py":"k in m"},"intent":["presence","missing key","键是否存在"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:sem.missing-is-nil"]},"examples":[{"code":"var m = new [];\n?. m.k = nil;\n?. m.k = 0;\n?. m.@has('k');\nm.k = 0;\n?. m.@has('k');\n","expect":"True\nTrue\nFalse\nTrue\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:pit.array-vs-map","@type":"fun:pitfall","name":"[] is a list, new [] is a map","description":"A list literal `[1, 2]` is ordered; `new [a: 1]` is a string-keyed map and `new []` is an empty map, but `new [1, 2]` is a list. Do not use `{}` for either.","level":0,"card":"[1,2,3] / new [k: v]","tags":["pitfall","data"],"transfer":{"js":"[] / {}","py":"[] / {}"},"intent":["array","dictionary","数组","字典"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.collection"]},"examples":[{"code":"var xs = [10, 20];\nvar m = new [a: 10];\n?. xs[1];\n?. m.a;\n","expect":"20\n10\n"},{"code":"var m = new [];\nm.k = 1;\n?. m.@toJson();\nvar xs = new [1, 2];\n?. xs.@toJson();\n","expect":"[k:1]\n[1,2]\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:pit.return-keyword","@type":"fun:pitfall","name":"result vs return","description":"Inside `fun`, assigning `result` sets the return value; `return expr;` returns immediately. A bare `return;` returns the current `result`, which may be stale.","level":0,"card":"result = expr; or return expr;","tags":["pitfall","function"],"transfer":{"js":"return x","py":"return x"},"intent":["return","返回"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:sem.result"]},"examples":[{"code":"fun f()\n  result = 1;\n  return 2;\n  result = 3;\nend fun;\n?. f();\n","expect":"2\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:tool.funcmd","@type":"fun:tool","name":"The fun command","description":"The command `fun file.fun` runs a script; `fun test` runs a package's tests; `fun pack` builds one executable; `fun package init` creates a manifest.","level":0,"card":"fun hello.fun / fun test / fun pack","tags":["tool","cli"],"transfer":{"js":"node hello.js","py":"python hello.py"},"intent":["run","test","build","运行","测试","打包"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:tool.package","fun:tool.test"]},"examples":[{"code":"?. 'Use: fun hello.fun';\n","expect":"Use: fun hello.fun\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:tool.test","@type":"fun:tool","name":"Tests","description":"Test files are `*_test.fun`; import `test.fun` and call `test('name', { assert.equal(a, b); });`. `fun test` runs each file in a child process.","level":1,"card":"use 'test.fun'; test('name', { assert.equal(a, b); });","tags":["tool","test"],"transfer":{"js":"test('name', () => expect(a).toBe(b))","py":"def test_name(): assert a == b"},"intent":["unit test","assertion","单元测试"],"relations":{"requires":["fun:tool.package"]},"examples":[{"code":"?. 'Write this in a *_test.fun file, then run: fun test';\n","expect":"Write this in a *_test.fun file, then run: fun test\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:tool.package","@type":"fun:tool","name":"Packages","description":"A project has a `package.fun` manifest. `fun package init/tidy/add/remove` creates and maintains it; `fun run` runs the manifest bin.","level":1,"card":"fun package init myapp && fun run","tags":["tool","package"],"transfer":{"js":"package.json / npm","py":"pyproject.toml / pip"},"intent":["package","dependency","包管理","依赖"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:tool.funcmd"]},"examples":[{"code":"?. 'fun package init myapp';\n","expect":"fun package init myapp\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:tool.fun-safe","@type":"fun:tool","name":"fun-safe","description":"A restricted build with native code, arbitrary memory access, and file/compile access removed. Use it for plugins and untrusted scripts.","level":1,"card":"fun-safe untrusted.fun","tags":["tool","security"],"intent":["sandbox","plugin","security","沙箱","安全"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:tool.funcmd"]},"examples":[{"code":"?. 'fun-safe script.fun';\n","expect":"fun-safe script.fun\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:tool.mt","@type":"fun:tool","name":"fun-mt and workers","description":"The `fun-mt` build is the opt-in multi-threaded build. A worker parses its own module and heap; results cross as strings, with `Shared` and `Channel` for named stores.","level":2,"card":"WorkerFile('job.fun', 'entry', args)","tags":["tool","concurrency"],"intent":["worker","thread","concurrency","并发","线程"],"relations":{"requires":["fun:platform.matrix"]},"examples":[{"code":"?. 'Requires fun-mt and use lib-worker.fun';\n","expect":"Requires fun-mt and use lib-worker.fun\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:platform.matrix","@type":"fun:platform","name":"Platforms","description":"Windows 95 through Windows 11, Linux x64/arm64 (glibc 2.17+), macOS x64/arm64, and nightly LoongArch64/riscv64 builds. About 0.3 MB, zero external dependencies.","level":1,"card":"Windows 95..11 / Linux / macOS / LoongArch64 / riscv64","tags":["platform"],"intent":["platform support","portability","平台","国产化"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:tool.fun-safe"]},"examples":[{"code":"var h = 'host'.arg().getJson(fd: true);\n?. h.os <> '';\n","expect":"True\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:module.lib-set","@type":"fun:module","name":"lib-set","description":"Collection helpers in pure Fun: `map`, `filter`, `find`, `sort`, `compose`, `range`, `@clone`, and more.","level":0,"card":"use 'lib-set.fun';","tags":["module","data"],"transfer":{"js":"Array.prototype.map/filter","py":"map/filter"},"intent":["list helpers","map filter","集合函数"],"examples":[{"code":"use 'lib-set.fun';\n?. ([1, 2, 3] | map(a -> a * 2)).@toJson();\n","expect":"[2,4,6]\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:module.lib-json","@type":"fun:module","name":"lib-json","description":"JSON and FD parse/stringify helpers. The underlying built-ins are `.getJson()` and `.@toJson()`, documented in `lib-json.fun`.","level":0,"card":"use 'lib-json.fun';","tags":["module","json"],"intent":["json helpers","JSON工具"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.json","fun:syntax.fd"]},"examples":[{"code":"var m = '{\"a\": 1}'.getJson(json: true);\n?. m.@toJson(json: true);\n","expect":"{\"a\":1}\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:module.runtime","@type":"fun:module","name":"runtime","description":"The calls `runtime.source()`, `runtime.stack()`, `runtime.lastError()` expose source locations, call stacks and the last caught error.","level":1,"card":"use 'runtime.fun'; runtime.lastError();","tags":["module","diagnostics"],"transfer":{"js":"new Error().stack","py":"traceback"},"intent":["stack trace","error details","调用栈","错误信息"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.try"]},"examples":[{"code":"use 'runtime.fun';\ntry\n  raise 'boom';\nexcept\n  var e = runtime.lastError();\n  ?. e.message = 'boom';\nend try;\n","expect":"True\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:module.fs","@type":"fun:module","name":"fs","description":"Portable filesystem helpers: `mkdirAll`, `list`, `walk`, `removeAll`, `tempFile`, `tempDir`, `atomicWrite` and byte streams.","level":1,"card":"use 'fs.fun'; fs.mkdirAll('out');","tags":["module","io"],"intent":["filesystem","directory","文件系统","目录"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:idiom.file-io"]},"examples":[{"code":"use 'fs.fun';\nvar d = fs.tempDir('fun-ontology-');\n?. d <> '';\nfs.removeAll(d);\n","expect":"True\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:module.cli","@type":"fun:module","name":"cli","description":"A command-line framework: subcommands, flags, aliases, env fallback, required flags, hooks and help.","level":2,"card":"use 'cli.fun';","tags":["module","cli"],"intent":["cli framework","flags","命令行框架"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:idiom.cli"]},"examples":[{"code":"?. 'See fun/lib/cli.fun';\n","expect":"See fun/lib/cli.fun\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:module.http-server","@type":"fun:module","name":"http-server","description":"An HTTP server with routing, path parameters, middleware, static files and a blocking poll loop. Handlers are `fun(req, res)`.","level":2,"card":"use 'http-server.fun'; var s = HttpServer(8080);","tags":["module","http","network"],"intent":["http server","rest api","web","HTTP服务","接口"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:module.http-client"]},"examples":[{"code":"?. 'See fun/lib/http-server.fun';\n","expect":"See fun/lib/http-server.fun\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:module.http-client","@type":"fun:module","name":"http-client","description":"An HTTP client with helpers for JSON, headers, timeouts and TLS. `use 'http-client.fun';`.","level":2,"card":"use 'http-client.fun';","tags":["module","http","network"],"transfer":{"js":"fetch(url)","py":"requests.get(url)"},"intent":["http request","fetch","HTTP客户端"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:module.http-server"]},"examples":[{"code":"?. 'See fun/lib/http-client.fun';\n","expect":"See fun/lib/http-client.fun\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:builtin.tojson","@type":"fun:builtin","name":"@toJson","description":"The built-in serializer. Default output is JSON-like with bare keys; `json: true` quotes keys, and `fd: true` emits FD.","level":0,"card":"value.@toJson(json: true);","tags":["builtin","data"],"transfer":{"js":"JSON.stringify(value)","py":"json.dumps(value)"},"intent":["serialize","stringify","序列化","转字符串"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.json","fun:syntax.fd"]},"examples":[{"code":"var m = new [a: 1, b: [2]];\n?. m.@toJson(json: true);\n","expect":"{\"a\":1,\"b\":[2]}\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:builtin.escape","@type":"fun:builtin","name":".escape()","description":"Decodes backslash escapes in a string: `'\\n'.escape()` is a newline, `'\\t'.escape()` a tab. Literals keep the backslash until `.escape()` is called.","level":0,"card":"'a\\nb'.escape()","tags":["builtin","text"],"transfer":{"js":"\"a\\nb\"","py":"\"a\\nb\"","c":"\"a\\nb\""},"intent":["escape","newline","转义","换行"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.string","fun:pit.backslash-escape"]},"examples":[{"code":"?. 'a\\nb'.length();\n?. 'a\\nb'.escape().length();\n?. 'x\\ty'.escape().length();\n","expect":"4\n3\n3\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:syntax.operator","@type":"fun:construct","name":"Operator overloading","description":"An operator is a field keyed by its symbol. In `this['#'] = you -> ...`, `me` is the receiver and `you` the right operand.","level":2,"card":"this['#'] = you -> (me + you) * me * you;","tags":["syntax","object"],"transfer":{"js":"Symbol.toPrimitive","py":"__add__"},"intent":["operator overloading","custom operator","运算符重载"],"relations":{"partOf":["fun:syntax.class"]},"examples":[{"code":"class Num(me)\n  this['#'] = you -> (me + you) * me * you;\nend class;\nvar n = Num(2);\n?. n .# 3;\n","expect":"30\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:sem.user-vs-builtin","@type":"fun:semantic","name":"User methods vs built-in methods","description":"Methods declared with `fun` inside a class are called as `obj.method()`. Engine methods are called as `obj.@method()`. The `@` is the dispatch marker, not part of the name.","level":1,"card":"obj.get() / obj.@toJson()","tags":["semantic","object"],"intent":["method call","builtin","方法","内建"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.method","fun:syntax.class"]},"examples":[{"code":"class Box(v)\n  var v = v;\n  fun get() result = v; end fun;\nend class;\nvar b = Box(7);\n?. b.get();\n","expect":"7\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:module.lib-fd","@type":"fun:module","name":"lib-fd","description":"FD parse and emit helpers. The underlying built-ins are `text.getJson(fd: true)` and `value.@toJson(fd: true)`.","level":1,"card":"use 'lib-fd.fun';","tags":["module","data"],"intent":["fd helpers","FD"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:syntax.fd"]},"examples":[{"code":"var m = 'a 1'.getJson(fd: true);\n?. m.a;\n","expect":"1\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:module.lib-type","@type":"fun:module","name":"lib-type","description":"Type conversion helpers: `toStr`, `toNum`, `toTime`, `toByte`, `toChar`, `fromByte`, `eq` and `type`.","level":1,"card":"use 'lib-type.fun';","tags":["module","type"],"intent":["type conversion","类型转换"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:sem.type"]},"examples":[{"code":"var n = 1;\n?. n.type();\n","expect":"3\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:module.lib-host","@type":"fun:module","name":"lib-host","description":"Host detection and libc binding: `LibC()`, `IsWindows()`, `HostCurrPath()`, and the `'host'.arg()` facts.","level":2,"card":"use 'lib-host.fun'; LibC().getapi(...)","tags":["module","native"],"intent":["libc","host info","主机信息"],"relations":{"seeAlso":["fun:idiom.ffi"]},"examples":[{"code":"use 'lib-host.fun';\nvar getpid = LibC().getapi('getpid', ':i');\n?. getpid() > 0;\n","expect":"True\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:module.lib-cwinapi","@type":"fun:module","name":"lib-cwinapi","description":"Windows helper: `CWin32API('user32.dll', 'int MessageBoxA(HWND, LPCSTR, LPCSTR, UINT);')` parses a C prototype and exposes named arguments.","level":2,"card":"CWin32API('user32.dll', prototype)","tags":["module","native","windows"],"intent":["win32 api","message box","Windows接口"],"relations":{"requires":["fun:platform.matrix"]},"examples":[{"code":"?. 'Windows only: use CWin32API(dll, prototype)';\n","expect":"Windows only: use CWin32API(dll, prototype)\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:module.lib-cstruct","@type":"fun:module","name":"lib-cstruct","description":"The call `CStruct('struct Point { int x; int y; };', [x: 3, y: 4])` computes offsets and padding and exposes a pointer-addressable buffer.","level":2,"card":"CStruct(declaration, values)","tags":["module","native"],"intent":["c struct","memory layout","C结构体"],"relations":{"requires":["fun:module.lib-cwinapi"]},"examples":[{"code":"?. 'Use CStruct(declaration, values) for C layouts';\n","expect":"Use CStruct(declaration, values) for C layouts\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:task.json-transform","@type":"fun:task","name":"Transform JSON","description":"Parse a JSON document, update a nested value, and emit JSON again.","level":0,"card":"parse -> mutate -> stringify","tags":["task","json"],"intent":["edit json","transform json","修改JSON"],"relations":{"requires":["fun:syntax.json","fun:idiom.json-roundtrip"]},"examples":[{"code":"var doc = '{\"items\": [{\"n\": 1}, {\"n\": 2}]}'.getJson(json: true);\nfor i = 0 to doc.items.@count() - 1 do\n  doc.items[i].n *= 10;\nend do;\n?. doc.@toJson(json: true);\n","expect":"{\"items\":[{\"n\":10},{\"n\":20}]}\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:task.hello-server","@type":"fun:task","name":"A tiny HTTP JSON endpoint","description":"Create `HttpServer(port)`, register a handler that writes JSON, and call `run()`. Requires a listening socket; not executed by the ontology checker.","level":1,"card":"HttpServer(8080).get('/health', handler)","tags":["task","http"],"intent":["web server","health endpoint","接口服务"],"relations":{"requires":["fun:module.http-server"]},"examples":[{"code":"use 'http-server.fun';\nfun health(req, res)\n  res.json([ok: true]);\nend fun;\nvar s = HttpServer(8080);\ns.get('/health', health);\ns.run();\n","runnable":false}]},{"@id":"fun:task.ffi-libc","@type":"fun:task","name":"Call a C function","description":"Bind a libc function by name and signature, then call it from Fun. Use CStruct/CWin32API when a struct or a Windows prototype is involved.","level":2,"card":"LibC().getapi('getpid', ':i')()","tags":["task","native"],"intent":["call c","ffi","调用C函数"],"relations":{"requires":["fun:idiom.ffi","fun:module.lib-cstruct"]},"examples":[{"code":"use 'lib-host.fun';\nvar getpid = LibC().getapi('getpid', ':i');\n?. getpid() > 0;\n","expect":"True\n"}]},{"@id":"fun:task.cli-args","@type":"fun:task","name":"Parse argv","description":"Read positional arguments with `i.arg()`, or use `Argv()`/`cli.fun` for flags and subcommands.","level":1,"card":"var a = 2.arg();","tags":["task","cli"],"intent":["command line args","命令行参数"],"relations":{"requires":["fun:idiom.cli"]},"examples":[{"code":"?. 0.arg().length() > 0;\n","expect":"True\n"}]}]}